# Enum nodes (Q52) — PARKED

> **Q90 (2026-08-06):** Catalog **`enum` is parked** — out of product direction.  
> Do **not** extend this model. Prefer hierarchy inheritance + attributes / Festwerte.  
> If the user asks to use enum again, follow [`.cursor/rules/parked-complex-types.mdc`](parked-complex-types.mdc) (warn first).  
> This file documents **legacy scaffold** shape until an explicit removal slice.

`enum` was a **Collection** kind: closed options, one scalar column (usually `text`).

## Correct shape (historical)

```text
Rolle                    ← field (type → enum catalog, or → concrete enum e.g. Bauart)
  └── Option             ← single column (type → text); names: Option | Spalte | Column | Wert
        ├── Empfänger    ← closed option leaf
        └── Lieferant
```

Concrete catalog example (BOM):

```text
enum (datatype)
  └── Bauart
        └── Option
              ├── 0201
              └── 0603
```

Field **Bauform** then has `type_id → Bauart` (not → catalog `enum`). Options are read from the **type** node.

## Defining Festwerte (scaffold)

- Catalog **`enum`** is only the kind marker — no value list UI there.
- On a **concrete enum** (`isConcreteEnum`: direct/nested specialization under catalog `enum`), the detail pane shows **Enum values** / Festwerte: add / remove / reorder labels.
- Persist via `Node_Type::set_enum_values` → ensure `Option` column → option leaf terms + `_wtt_position` (not `_wtt_enum_values` meta).
- AJAX: `wtt_set_enum_values`. Attribute Festwert pickers for concrete-enum types use the same `get_enum_options` list.

## Wrong / incomplete

- Options as **direct** children of the field (no `Option` column) — renderer still falls back, but prefer the column shape.
- Typing the field as `text` while putting options underneath — that is not an enum.
- Putting DigiKey/Mouser samples under catalog `enum` — those belong under **Lieferanten**, not enum.

## Rendering

- Dedicated **`EnumRenderer`** in `wtt-node-render.js` (select in edit; label in display).
- PHP exposes **`enumOptions`** via `Node_Type::get_enum_options` on `get_node` and table band fields.
- Preview / table cells go through **Registry** (`renderFieldView` / table cell `renderContent`) — do not paint a plain text input for `typeKey === 'enum'`.

## Do / don’t (legacy only)

- **Don’t** extend Enum UI, Option column tooling, or `EnumRenderer` for product work (**Q90**).
- **Don’t** special-case Rolle/Bauart by name.
- **Do** prefer hierarchy + attributes / Default value (Festwert meta) for closed values.
- Scaffold may still paint `EnumRenderer` until an explicit removal slice.
